# Git Commit Messages

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) in **English**, aligned with [clowder-ai](https://github.com/zts212653/clowder-ai) style.

## Format

```text
<type>(<scope>): <short summary>

[optional body]
```

## Rules

- Subject in English only; imperative mood (`add`, not `added` / `Adding`)
- Types: `feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `perf` | `refactor` | `test` | `chore` | `ci`
- Scope = package or domain: `core` | `api` | `mcp` | `web` | `harness` | `openspec` | feature id when relevant
- Keep the subject concise; put rationale and details in the body when needed
- Pass the message via HEREDOC when committing; do not use Chinese in the subject

## Examples

```text
feat(core): add verify-loop state machine
fix(mcp): pass bearer auth to tool handlers
docs(adr): record postgres-over-sqlite decision
test(harness): add summary-vs-verify holdout cases
chore(repo): scaffold pnpm workspace and docker compose
```
